{"step_index":9882,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-25T13:28:10Z","thinking":"Planning the `gemini_vision_extractor.py` module, the core functions are: a file hash computation (SHA-256) and a strategy for controlled cache storage. The file hash serves as a unique identifier for PDF files. Organized cache storage prevents haphazard temporary file placement.\n\n\nThe system will establish a consistent cache structure based on process context or a fallback directory outside the process space if needed. A manifest file will track processing status and page completion, enabling quick resumption from prior work. The extraction will first attempt to load fully cached results for immediate return.\n\nIf a full cache isn't available, pending pages, those missing results or needing WebP rendering, are identified. WebP images will be generated if not present, and then results will be gathered for the identified pending pages.\n\n\nNow focusing on processing image data, preparing to send requests to an image analysis endpoint with base64 encoded image data and a specific prompt designed for pharmaceutical extraction. The response will be parsed as JSON, validated for the presence of extracted items, and then saved to a designated file. Page completion is tracked and the manifest updated accordingly.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nGemini Vision Extraction Engine.\\nExtracts pharmaceutical items from PDF files page-by-page using Google AI Studio Vision Gateway.\\nFeatures:\\n- WebP high-resolution compressed rendering (pypdfium2 at scale 2.5)\\n- Process-isolated structured cache (manifest.json, pages/, results/)\\n- Full resume & interruption capability (resumes from incomplete page)\\n- SHA-256 fingerprinting for instant cache reloads\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nimport base64\\nimport hashlib\\nimport json\\nimport re\\nimport time\\nfrom datetime import datetime\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nimport pypdfium2 as pdfium\\nimport requests\\n\\n\\ndef _compute_file_hash(filepath: Path) -> str:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Computes SHA-256 checksum of a file.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    hasher = hashlib.sha256()\\n    with open(filepath, \\\"rb\\\") as f:\\n        while chunk := f.read(65536):\\n            hasher.update(chunk)\\n    return hasher.hexdigest()\\n\\n\\ndef _get_cache_dir(filepath: Path) -> Path:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Finds or creates an organized cache directory for this file.\\n    If the file is inside a process folder (data/processes/PROC-XXX),\\n    places cache under data/processes/PROC-XXX/cache/vision/<file_slug>_<hash[:10]>.\\n    Otherwise places it under <parent>/.vision_cache/<file_slug>_<hash[:10]>.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    filepath = Path(filepath).resolve()\\n    file_hash = _compute_file_hash(filepath)\\n    file_slug = re.sub(r\\\"[^\\\\w\\\\-]\\\", \\\"_\\\", filepath.stem)[:25]\\n    folder_name = f\\\"{file_slug}_{file_hash[:10]}\\\"\\n\\n    # Check if inside a process directory\\n    parts = filepath.parts\\n    proc_idx = -1\\n    for i, p in enumerate(parts):\\n        if p.startswith(\\\"PROC-\\\"):\\n            proc_idx = i\\n            break\\n\\n    if proc_idx != -1:\\n        proc_root = Path(*parts[:proc_idx + 1])\\n        cache_dir = proc_root / \\\"cache\\\" / \\\"vision\\\" / folder_name\\n    else:\\n        cache_dir = filepath.parent / \\\".vision_cache\\\" / folder_name\\n\\n    (cache_dir / \\\"pages\\\").mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\\n    (cache_dir / \\\"results\\\").mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\\n    return cache_dir\\\n<truncated 10136 bytes>","Description":"\"Create gemini_vision_extractor.py for robust page-by-page vision extraction with resume and isolated cache\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"d:\\\\AI_Engineer\\\\Pharmacy-agy-vision\\\\src\\\\extract\\\\gemini_vision_extractor.py\"","toolAction":"\"Creating gemini_vision_extractor.py\"","toolSummary":"\"Write gemini_vision_extractor.py\"